{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>A guilt offering, a guilt offering.</b> Rashi explained: to bring the guilt offering of a designated female servant, that it be a ram in its second year. But since it is called איל (ram), it is obvious that it is in its second year — and what force is there in the guilt offering of trespasses compared to other guilt offerings? Furthermore, it says לאלתר (immediately); one might think I include the guilt offering of a nazirite and the guilt offering of a leper — therefore it says אשם הוא (it is a guilt offering). But how can you include the guilt offering of a leper — is it not written concerning it כבש (lamb), which means in its first year? Therefore one may say that we read as Rashi explained: to bring the guilt offering of a designated female servant, that it be of two shekels' value — for we find nowhere in all the Torah written 'two shekels' except for the guilt offering of trespasses. And thus it is in the Tanchuma: from where do we know for the guilt offering of a designated female servant that he may not bring except with the silver of shekels? It says אשם אשם (a guilt offering, a guilt offering)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:11.232870541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}